{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets (excl. territories) and the 2025 population from the census file's own 'United States' row : how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786912063249},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Get the total number of farmers markets from the first CSV (excluding territories)\n2. Get the 2025 US population from the second CSV (from the 'United States' row)\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents to 4 decimal places\n4. Provide one confident sentence with verified facts\n\nFollowing the xorq analyst instructions, I should:\n1. First check for semantic models with `xorq_semantic_models`\n2. Check existing aliases with `xorq_catalog_list_aliases`\n3. Ingest the data sources into the catalog if needed\n4. Compute values with `xorq_select`\n5. Verify everything with `xorq_verify`\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog setup.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking the catalog and then ingesting these data sources."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_014S9RdjfGE8dArGadBCfhdb","name":"xorq_catalog_info","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01BrkLFkSdXQqJiY1LfZyhE4","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01VCUEk7bMZJxQXwGXR4jMUE","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":380,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8173,"totalTokens":8563,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0019000000000000002,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01021625,"total":0.01212625},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":185},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912063261,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74J5a5bYRyziFebo1MJ","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_014S9RdjfGE8dArGadBCfhdb","toolName":"xorq_catalog_info","content":[{"type":"text","text":"path:    /private/tmp/trial-pi-46-80j2zifa/.xorq/catalog\ncommit:  568f714fbc0e\nremotes: (none)\nentries: 0\naliases: 0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912068786},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01BrkLFkSdXQqJiY1LfZyhE4","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No semantic models in this catalog — fall back to the ordinary ingest/compose flow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912068787},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01VCUEk7bMZJxQXwGXR4jMUE","toolName":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No aliases.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912068787},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest the two data sources. Let me create build scripts for both datasets. I'll need to:\n\n1. Ingest the farmers markets CSV\n2. Ingest the census population CSV\n3. Then compose them together to calculate the per-capita metric\n\nLet me start by creating the build scripts in `.xorq/scripts/`.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest both data sources. Let me create build scripts for the farmers markets and census data."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Damew6GP8vyfRmjy64BAbx","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p .xorq/scripts"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":179,"cacheRead":