","toolCallId":"toolu_01L4pSQ3uyqKaLovgqxZLngQ","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_name\"\n\"California\"\n\"Tennessee\"\n\"Louisiana\"\n\"New York\"\n\"Georgia\"\n\"Texas\"\n\"North Carolina\"\n\"Washington\"\n\"Montana\"\n\"Michigan\"\n\"Oregon\"\n\"Oklahoma\"\n\"New Jersey\"\n\"Alaska\"\n\"Mississippi\"\n\"Puerto Rico\"\n\"Virginia\"\n\"Ohio\"\n\"Rhode Island\"\n\"Wisconsin\"\n\"Indiana\"\n\"Maryland\"\n\"Arkansas\"\n\"Hawaii\"\n\"Massachusetts\"\n\"Connecticut\"\n\"Vermont\"\n\"North Dakota\"\n\"Virgin Islands\"\n\"Pennsylvania\"\n\"Illinois\"\n\"Florida\"\n\"Missouri\"\n\"Alabama\"\n\"New Mexico\"\n\"Minnesota\"\n\"Kentucky\"\n\"Colorado\"\n\"Kansas\"\n\"West Virginia\"\n\"Wyoming\"\n\"District Of Columbia\"\n\"Delaware\"\n\"Iowa\"\n\"Idaho\"\n\"Maine\"\n\"Arizona\"\n\"South Carolina\"\n\"Nebraska\"\n\"New Hampshire\"\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912123993},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see the territories:\n- Puerto Rico\n- Virgin Islands\n\nThese are the territories I need to exclude. Now I'll calculate:\n1. Total farmers markets excluding Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands\n2. Use the 2025 population from the census (341,784,857)\n3. Calculate per 100,000 residents\n\nLet me create a build script to compute the metric or just use xorq_select to get the sum and do the calculation.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01DWkQofTbturNMn9ZzTEajb","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.filter(source.state_name != 'Puerto Rico').filter(source.state_name != 'Virgin Islands').aggregate(total_markets=source.farmers_markets.sum())"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":249,"cacheRead":19407,"cacheWrite":402,"totalTokens":20070,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.001245,"cacheRead":0.0019407,"cacheWrite":0.0005025,"total":0.0037002000000000003},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":107},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912123994,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74NaXEUMLSdMAub5HiG","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01DWkQofTbturNMn9ZzTEajb","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"total_markets\"\n7942\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912129488},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! So we have:\n- Total farmers markets (excluding territories): 7,942\n- 2025 US population: 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to calculate: (7942 / 341784857) * 100000\n\nI should create a build script that computes this metric, or I can use xorq_select to compute it. However, to be thorough and create a verifiable metric, I should create a proper build script that joins these two values and computes the ratio. Let me create that script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a build script to compute the farmers markets per 100,000 residents metric by joining both datasets:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_012sEJ2FT9qKAMgehHbqNn7X","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"farmers_markets\", storage_options=so)\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"census_population\", storage_options=so)\n\n# Calculate total farmers markets excluding territories (Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands)\nfact_totals = (\n    fact.filter(fact.state_name != 'Puerto Rico')\n        .filter(fact.state_name != 'Virgin Islands')\n        .aggregate(total_farmers_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum())\n        .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Get US population for 2025\nus_population = (\n    ref.filter(ref.NAME == 'United States')\n        .select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n        .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Join and compute the ratio per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    fact_totals.join(us_population, fact_totals.k == us_population.k)\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=fact_totals.total_farmers_markets / us_population.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select('total_farmers_markets', 'POPESTIMATE2025', 'markets_per_100k')\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":747,"cacheRead":19809,"cacheWrite":295,"totalTokens":20863,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0037350000000000005,"cacheRead":0.0019809000000000003,"cacheWrite":0.00036875,"total":0.006096650000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":123},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912129488,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74NzsCZ2mXUu3CRrBR7","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_012sEJ2FT9qKAMgehHbqNn7X","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1431 bytes to .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912138505},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me build this script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01K71RiyqPahStUU3Gbx3ETV","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-46-80j2zifa && xorq build .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/metric_bp.txt && cat /tmp/metric_bp.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-